       'Establish the facts in a timeline: the event, when the controller became aware (the moment that starts the clock), discovery, containment, the categories and approximate numbers of data subjects and records, the data types, the breach type (confidentiality, integrity, availability) and the processor involved, if any.',
       'Assess the risk to the rights and freedoms of individuals with the EDPB factors: type of breach, nature and sensitivity of the data, ease of identification, severity of consequences, special characteristics of the subjects and of the controller, number affected; conclude unlikely risk, risk or high risk.',
       'Map the conclusion to the duties: documentation in the breach register in every case (Article 33(5)); notification to the authority unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk (Article 33(1)); communication to the data subjects where the risk is likely high (Article 34), unless an Article 34(3) exception applies.',
